# 2. Product Goals

## 2.1 Primary Goals

The MVP must:

- Allow visitors to browse public problems without logging in.
- Require Google authentication before users can interact.
- Make publishing a problem possible in under 60 seconds when the user has their content ready.
- Provide anonymous public identities by default.
- Support five problem categories.
- Allow users to select a city.
- Include a basic discussion and upvoting system.
- Display open and resolved statuses.
- Include reporting and a basic moderation workflow from day one.
- Provide an attractive, responsive interface.
- Remain lightweight and inexpensive to operate.

## 2.2 Success Metrics

| Metric | Initial Target |
|---|---|
| Time to publish | Under 60 seconds |
| Registration friction | Google sign-in without a separate password |
| Posting completion | At least 70% of users who start posting complete it |
| Duplicate votes | Prevented by database constraints |
| Mobile usability | All core features work on smartphones |
| Reporting | Every report enters a review workflow |
| Core reliability | No critical failures in authentication, posting, or commenting |

These are initial product targets, not existing performance results.

