# 10. Problem Details and Comments

## 10.1 Problem Details Page

Display:
- Full title and description.
- City and category.
- Anonymous author.
- Publication date.
- Optional image.
- Upvote action.
- Comment action.
- Share action.
- Report action.
- Resolution status.
- Comments.

Public posts and approved comments should be readable without login.

## 10.2 Comments

Authenticated users can:
- Add comments.
- Read existing comments.
- Report inappropriate comments.

Requirements:
- Maximum comment length: 1,500 characters.
- Anonymous display username.
- Timestamp.
- Input validation.
- Rate limiting.
- Basic moderation.

Use a simple chronological comment list.

Do not implement nested comment trees in the MVP.

If no comments exist, display:

"No advice yet. You could be the first to help."

## 10.3 Upvotes

Rules:
- One active upvote per user per post.
- Users can remove their upvote.
- Guests can see vote counts but cannot vote.
- Database constraints prevent duplicate votes.
- Counts must reflect actual vote records.

Do not implement downvotes initially.

## 10.4 Sharing

Every approved public post should have a permanent URL.

Support:
- Copy link.
- Native device sharing where available.
- Opening the post without requiring login.

Never include private user information in the shared URL.

