# 22. MVP Acceptance Criteria

The first version is complete when:

### Browsing
- Visitors can browse approved public posts without signing in.
- Visitors can read comments.
- City and category filters work.

### Authentication
- Google sign-in works.
- Anonymous usernames are generated automatically.
- Public content does not expose real names or emails.
- Users return to their intended action after signing in.

### Posting
- Authenticated users can create valid posts.
- Required fields are validated.
- Optional image uploads work securely.
- Posts appear after approval.
- Users can find their own posts.

### Community
- Users can comment.
- Users can upvote.
- Duplicate votes are prevented.
- Authors can mark their own posts as resolved.
- Users cannot modify other people's content.

### Moderation
- Users can report posts and comments.
- Reports enter the moderation queue.
- Unauthorized users cannot access the admin interface.
- Unapproved content is not publicly exposed.

### Responsive Design
- The interface works on mobile and desktop.
- Forms remain usable with the mobile keyboard open.
- Navigation does not cover content.
- Loading, empty, success, and error states are handled.

